		</section>
		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">4</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following is what I came up with.
1. Read the number of dials
2. Read the max limit of the dial
3. Read the number of inputs for which we have to increase correspoding dial value by 1
4. Write down the max dial as 0
5. Create an empty array
6. Assign 0 as default value to the each element of the array till the number of dials
7. Read the next number from the inputs
8. Increment the corresponding dial value by 1
9. Check if the value of the dial reached the max limit of the dial
10. If yes, update the value of max dial to the dial that reached the max limit of the dial and stop reading inputs by using break
11. If no, repeat steps 7, 8, 9, 10 and 11 until you reach the end of the inputs
12. By the end, max dial will be the dial that first reached the max limit of the dial as per problem statement</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">117.97172873679494</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">1638.9757660613407</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">319.47475971991173</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">302.6206116784682</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">Following is what I came up with.
1. Read the number of dials
2. Read the max limit of the dial
3. Read the number of inputs for which we have to increase correspoding dial value by 1
4. Write down the max dial as 0
